    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\">Features of extranodal marginal zone lymphoma of mucosa-associated lymphoid tissue (EMZL) by anatomical site</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Judith A. Ferry",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 697.4pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"930\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 133.8pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"178\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Site</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.8pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Proportion of head and neck EMZLs</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.8pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"202\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Risk factors</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 143.2pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"191\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Distinctive features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 164.8pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"220\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Recurrent genetic changes</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 133.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"178\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Ocular adnexa</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>(orbital soft tissue &gt; conjunctiva &gt; lacrimal apparatus)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">60%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"202\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Most are sporadic</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>Chlamydia psittaci</em>, geographical variation</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">HCV, geographical variation</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">IgG4-related disease, few cases</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 143.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"191\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Patients with orbital lymphoma present with exophthalmos, ptosis, diplopia; conjunctival lymphoma often forms a salmon patch</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 164.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"220\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal;\">TNFAIP3</em> (<em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal;\">A20</em>) inactivation (association with IGH4-34 usage)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal;\">TB1LXR1</em> mutation (association with IGHV3-23 usage)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">t(14;18)(q32;q21)/<span style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: italic;\">IGH::</span><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal;\">MALT1</em></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Trisomy&nbsp;3</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Trisomy&nbsp;8</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 133.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"178\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Salivary glands</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">(parotid &gt;&gt; submandibular &gt; minor salivary glands)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">30&ndash;40%</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"202\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Sj&ouml;gren syndrome</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">HCV, geographical variation</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">IgG4-related disease, few cases</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 143.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"191\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Lymphomas arise from LESA; haloes of monocytoid B&nbsp;cells form around LELs then expand and become confluent; BCRs often have rheumatoid factor activity</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 164.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"220\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">TBL1XR1</span></em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> mutation</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">GPR34</span></em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> mutation or translocation</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">t(14;18)(q32;q21)/<span style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: italic;\">IGH::</span><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal;\">MALT1</em></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Trisomy&nbsp;3</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Trisomy&nbsp;8</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Preferential usage of IGHV1-69</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 133.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"178\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Waldeyer ring</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Rare</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"202\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Most are sporadic</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 143.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"191\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Lymphoma can mimic non-neoplastic tonsillar or nasopharyngeal tissue, because intraepithelial B&nbsp;cells are normally abundant in these sites</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 164.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"220\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Limited data</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 133.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"178\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Oral cavity</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Rare</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"202\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Most are sporadic</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 143.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"191\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Subset of cases arises from minor salivary glands</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 164.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"220\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Rare report of t(11;18)/<em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal;\">BIRC3</em><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: italic;\">::</span><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal;\">MALT1</em> fusion</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 133.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"178\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Larynx</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Rare</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"202\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Sj&ouml;gren syndrome, systemic lupus erythematosus, or rheumatoid arthritis, rare cases</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 143.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"191\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Most cases are supraglottic</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 164.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"220\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Limited data</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 133.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"178\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Sinonasal region</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Rare</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"202\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Unknown</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 143.2pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"191\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 164.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"220\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Limited data</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">BCR, B-cell receptor (immunoglobulin); LEL, lymphoepithelial lesion; LESA, lymphoepithelial sialadenitis.</p>",
